WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.436
The first job is getting the work done.

2
00:00:03.486 --> 00:00:08.741
When people are not sure what is expected, work comes in late or gets redone,

3
00:00:08.791 --> 00:00:12.805
and you find out on the due date. Four habits prevent that.

4
00:00:12.855 --> 00:00:16.800
Plan it: decide what matters, who owns it, and what gives.

5
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:22.655
Say it: what is expected, by when, and what good looks like, out loud and in writing.

6
00:00:22.705 --> 00:00:28.097
Check it: look at the work before it is due, while there is still time to help.

7
00:00:28.147 --> 00:00:33.125
Fix it: when the same thing breaks twice, find the cause, not the person.

8
00:00:33.175 --> 00:00:37.810
And one habit to stop: doing the work yourself because it is faster.

9
00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.874
For example: a monthly report your team owns is due Friday.

10
00:00:41.924 --> 00:00:47.729
The person who builds it has not mentioned it in two weeks, and a director is asking.

11
00:00:47.779 --> 00:00:51.242
Building it yourself Thursday night is the old job.

12
00:00:51.292 --> 00:00:58.475
A fifteen-minute check-in on Wednesday, where the report stands and what she needs, is the manager’s job.

13
00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:03.710
This week: pick one person and confirm, out loud, what they own and by when.

